==============================================================================
THE OLD NORMALIZER WAS TRUNCATING STREETS -- 5,134 rows
==============================================================================
Not a cosmetic signature bump. The old unit pattern had no word boundary, so a
designator spelled inside an ordinary word was read as one and the street was
cut there. In 5,134 rows the old street_key is a strict prefix of the new:

  street                 old key            new key
  20 GILSLAND FARM RD    20 GILSLAND FA     20 GILSLAND FARM RD
  34 WING FARM PKWY      34 WING FA         34 WING FARM PKWY
  13 COUNTRY CHARM RD    13 COUNTRY CHA     13 COUNTRY CHARM RD
  356 VLY STRM CIR       356 VLY ST         356 VLY STRM CIR
  16 INDIAN STRM RD      16 INDIAN ST       16 INDIAN STRM RD
  74 HORSE FARM RD       74 HORSE FA        74 HORSE FARM RD

RM inside FARM, ST inside STRM, CHA from CHARM. Every farm road in the
reference was keyed to its own truncation and could not match on street. This
is npmatch's 27,954-row false-extraction bug (11.3% of extractions, masking the
real unit on 3,636) as it landed in pfmatch's own reference.

