STILL OPEN
==============================================================================
* Every measurement taken against the old reference is now on a different
  footing. BASELINE-2026-10B and the triangulation run (population
  cb3c78ff0f1a9546, dev/TRI-V2-BUILD.log) were matched against the old bundle.
  Nothing is retracted by this rebuild, but a rerun will not reproduce them and
  should not be expected to.
* REF-augmented.rds is matchdb's Phase 2 gate target ("md_compile(*-observed)
  must reproduce this", dev/build-baseline.R). That target has now moved.
  matchdb re-froze its own Phase 1 baseline on the fixed normalizer in its
  PR #16; this is the same move on pfmatch's side, and matchdb's Phase 2
  comparison needs the new bundle, not the kept one.
* pf_variants still records keys under v1-6dcb298522cc5118, so
  test-variants.R's pinned test skips. Rebuilding it would pair new keys with
  match statuses produced under the old normalizer, so it is left alone until
  the match is rerun.
* REF-active.rds, REF-unified.rds and REF-augmented-collapsed.rds are all
  still on the old normalizer and unstamped.
